  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA cold front will slowly move through the region this morning. \nIt will take a bit of time for the cooler and drier airmass to \nadvect in behind the front. So, a warm Thursday is expected as \nhighs push 80. Low temperatures do trend cooler tonight with\nclear skies under high pressure. Friday looks like a winner with\nsunshine and cooler temperatures as well. Will have to monitor\nthe potential for some wind gusts around 20-25 mph later this\nafternoon and evening based on model soundings. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure moves offshore which will begin the process of\nadvecting warmer and moister air into the region. A warm front\nlooks to be a focus for some scattered showers and isolated\nthunderstorms Saturday afternoon through early Sunday. Lift \nwith a weak cold frontal passage could be enough for a few \nadditional showers and thunderstorms Sunday afternoon. \nThe warm front has trended slightly faster from previous\nupdates.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nA quick break with high pressure looks to occur Monday.\nTemperatures look to peak on Tuesday as modeled 925 mb\ntemperatures suggest highs well into the 80's. There is a fairly\nlarge six standard deviation spread with temperatures in the \nECMWF suite. However, thinking is still that the NBM will trend \nwarmer as we get closer to Tuesday. Ensemble guidance is in \nfairly good agreement the next chance for showers and \nthunderstorms holds off till later Tuesday into Wednesday.",
